  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1031 PM CDT Thu May 14 2026\n\nIt's only a matter of time before Nashville hits its first 90 degree \nday of the year, and that day likely is Sunday with the NBM giving a \nhigh chance (80-90%) of hitting that mark. And temperatures will \nonly go up from there as summer-like temperatures stay in place \nthrough the first half of next week. Monday looks like the warmest \nday as highs reach into the low-90s for locations west of the \nPlateau. As far as any appreciable rain goes, we will still have to \nwait until the middle of next week. By Tuesday, a large trough with \na front will be approaching from the west, increasing our rain \nchances. Best rain chances of 50-70% right now are on Wednesday. As \nfar as rain amounts go, higher amounts currently favor the northwest \nwhere probability of exceeding one half inch is at 40-60% with a 20-\n40% chance of exceeding one inch.",
